## C2 — calibration (lowest assigned axis): the round-82 record's six declared facts re-derive at the sealed revision or are answered by dated value-bound corrections, with population facts bound at freeze

Frozen predicate (this block is the counter's `PREDICATE`, the receipt label and the SCORECARD row):

> `python3 tools/round83-selfrecord-round82.py --repo <lane>` prints one `SELFRECORD_R82 claims=6
> mismatches=0 corrected=3 unbacked=0` line and exits 0 only when each of the six facts the round-82
> self-record declares re-derives from the tree at the sealed revision
> `b1ba614b51255a3dcfe3e0946f32f8e31bd65c09` and matches the same fact re-derived at the graded tip,
> or is answered by exactly one committed `corrected F<n> old=<token> new=<token> at=<40-hex>
> date=<ISO> fix=<path>` block in `corpus/lessons/round-83.md` `## Corrections` whose `old` is the
> sealed declared token, whose `at` is the sealed revision, whose `new` equals the fact's tip witness
> token, and whose `fix` path's tip bytes contain the literal `new` token as a whole token **outside
> any correction-restatement region** (a `#### round-<N> correction` block or a `LOG-CORRECTION`
> line), while the token also occurs at the tip in at least one file outside `corpus/lessons/`; a
> token that appears only under `corpus/lessons/`, or only inside a correction-restatement region, is
> `unbacked` — the correction container's `fix` leg rejects a token that appears only in the lesson
> itself. It exits 1 naming every unanswered fact. A fact that holds at the sealed revision needs no
> correction; a correction for a holding or unnamed fact, a duplicated correction, a correction
> outside `## Corrections`, a wrong `at`, a wrong `old`, or a `fix` whose tip bytes lack the token is
> `unbacked` and is also a mismatch.

